  <p class="note">If damp or cracks need fixing, that comes first. To sell or let you also need an energy certificate (<em>certificado energético</em>).</p>
  <p>Don’t forget the windows: single glazing in an old frame loses more heat than a whole wall. See <a href="/en/costs/windows-and-frames/">windows and frames</a>. And with insulation a <a href="/en/costs/air-conditioning-and-heat-pumps/">heat pump or air conditioning</a> runs far more efficiently; read also <a href="/en/guides/heating-and-cooling-spain/">heating and cooling in Spain</a>.</p>

  <p><strong>Want your house insulated?</strong> We find where your house loses most heat and make sure the work is done properly, from roof to wall lining. <a href="/en/request/?dienst=renovatie">Tell us what you would like to tackle</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="damp">Insulating without damp problems</h2>
  <p>An insulated house is more airtight. That is good for warmth, but moisture has to go somewhere. So pay attention to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Ventilation</strong>: trickle vents in the windows or an extractor in the bathroom and kitchen.</li>
    <li><strong>Fixing the causes of damp first</strong>: a leaking roof, a broken downpipe or rising damp.</li>
    <li><strong>The right material</strong>: on old stone walls, use breathable systems.</li>
    <li><strong>A house that stands empty for long periods</strong> benefits from a dehumidifier or regular airing. That can be arranged through <a href="/en/key-holding/">key holding</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="order">Where to start</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>The <strong>roof</strong>, especially over the top floor or a roof terrace.</li>
    <li>The <strong>windows</strong> if they are still single glazed.</li>
    <li>The <strong>outside walls</strong> of the rooms you use most in winter, for example with a wall lining.</li>
    <li>Only then choose the <strong>heating</strong>: an insulated house needs a smaller system.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="note">This guide gives general information for the Axarquía in November 2026. Rules may change.</p>
</Guide>
